-- title:
--   Rigidified lift over an Artinian base with prescribed period
-- statement:
--   The statement is an existence result for rigidified fake elliptic curves over an Artinian local base, formulated inside a large Čerednik–Drinfeld frame whose data are all carried as hypotheses. The hypotheses fall into the following groups; each group is described, and the ones consisting of many clauses are summarised as indicated.
--
--   **Arithmetic base.** Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r \neq r$, and a nonzero squarefree $N$ divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$ (`hrr`, `hrN`, `hrbarN`, `hN`). A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), an irreducible element $\pi$ with $\mathcal O$ $\pi$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), residue ring of cardinality $r$ (`hres`) and $(r) = (\pi)$ (`hunr`), together with a characteristic-zero fraction field $K_0$ of $\mathcal O$. A characteristic-zero $\mathcal O$-domain $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ (written `Onr`) with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, such that $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), that ideal is maximal (`hOnr_max`), every element of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies a monic $\mathcal O$-polynomial modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial of positive degree over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ (`hFr`). A homomorphism $\mathrm{vdet} : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (multiplicatively written) with $\mathrm{vdet}(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$ (`hvdet`).
--
--   **Indefinite side and moduli.** Rationals $a,b$ with `hB`: $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ satisfies $0<a$ or $0<b$ and is locally a division algebra at exactly the height-one primes containing $r$ or $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda$ (`hΛ`); a scheme $\mathcal X$ with a morphism $f$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and a point map $\mathrm{pt}$ on fake elliptic curves with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure, such that `h𝒳` holds: $\mathcal X$ is a coarse moduli space (invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with base change, bijectivity on geometric points of algebraically closed fields, and the universal property). An integer $n \geq 3$ prime to $r$, to $\bar r$ and to $N$ (`hn`, `hrn`, `hrbarn`, `hnN`); a scheme $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point map $\mathrm{ptF}$ on curves with full level $n$ which is a fine moduli space (`hM`: iso-invariance, base change, surjectivity and injectivity of the point map), a group $G$ acting by automorphisms $\rho$ of $M$ with labels $\chi : G \to \Lambda$ satisfying `hρ` (the action is over the base, realises the twisting of full-level structures by $\chi(g)$, and the labels are multiplicative, unital, surjective and injective modulo $n$). A forgetful morphism $p : M \to \mathcal X$ over the base (`hp`), invariant under $G$ (`hρp`) and compatible with the two point maps (`hp_pt`). For each prime $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$ a coarse moduli scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell$ for curves with extra level $\ell$ (`h𝒴`) together with degeneracy morphisms $d_0(\ell), d_1(\ell) : \mathcal Y_\ell \to \mathcal X$ over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) whose effect on points is forgetting the extra level, respectively passing to an $\ell$-isogenous curve (`hd₀`, `hd₁`). Endomorphisms $a_r, a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ over the base (`harf`, `harbarf`) inducing on points the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $r$, respectively at $\bar r$ (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **Definite side.** Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with `hdef`: $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$ and $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ is locally a division algebra at exactly the primes containing $\bar r$. A maximal order $\Lambda_1$ and an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ with $R_1 \leq \Lambda_1$ (`hΛ₁`, `hR₁`, `hRΛ₁`); an adelic unit $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ (`hn₁`) such that $R_1 \cap n_1 R_1 n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`); an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ into $M_2(K_0)$ (`hι₀`); a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathbb Z$ containing $r$ (`hv`). A subgroup $\Gamma^{t}$ of the unit group consisting exactly of the units lying in the local unit boxes of $R_1$ away from $v$ (`hΓt`); families $s$ and $s^{f}$ indexed by the primes $\ell \notin\{r,\bar r\}$ with `hs` (four clauses: $s^f_\ell$ has component $s_\ell$ at every prime not containing $r$, component $1$ at the primes containing $r$, the diagonal $\ell$ times $(s^f_\ell)^{-1}$ lies in the level Hecke set of $\Lambda_1$ and $R_1 \cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ at $\ell$ when $\ell \mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell) = \ell$); the groups $\Gamma^{t}_\ell = \Gamma^{t} \cap s_\ell \Gamma^{t} s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`); and a unit $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma^{t}$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   **Data over the residue field.** The hypothesis `hΛℤ` that all rational integers lie in $\Lambda$; a map $\mathrm{coord} : \Lambda \to \mathbb Z_{r^2}^{\,2}$ (Witt vectors over $\mathbb F_{r^2}$, twice) which is an order coordinate (`hcoord`: additive, sends $1$ to $(1,0)$, multiplicative in the Frobenius-twisted sense, injective, with dense image and with the trace clause). Over the residue ring $k_0 = O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$: a fake elliptic curve $A_0$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of rank $2$ along the unit section of $A_0$, and `hA₀` that $\theta_0$ are formal coordinates for the group law of $A_0$ with formal group $X_0$ and that the $\Lambda$-action is given in these coordinates by $\mathrm{coord}$. Families $e, e' : \Gamma^{t} \to \operatorname{End}(A_0)$ with $e\gamma$ over the base (`he`) and degrees $\deg$, subject to: `hE1` (each pair $(e\gamma, e'\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg \gamma}$ preserving the level structure); `hE1mul` (multiplicativity up to multiplication by powers of $r$); `hE1sc` (rational-integer $\gamma$ act by that integer up to powers of $r$); `hE1'` (conversely, if $e\gamma$ becomes multiplication by a positive integer after twisting by a power of $r$, then $\gamma$ is a rational scalar); `hE2` (for every injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $X_0$-action and $\varpi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $e\gamma$ is induced on $\theta_0$ by an element $\varepsilon$ of that centraliser with $E_0\varepsilon = r^{k_\gamma}\,g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$); `hE3` (every full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$ admits labels $\mathrm{lab} : \Gamma^t \to \Lambda$ describing the action of $e\gamma$ on it, multiplicative and unital modulo $n$); `hE4` (on every geometric pullback of $A_0$ to an algebraically closed field, each level-preserving isogeny pair of $r$-power degree is, up to powers of $r$, the pullback of some $e\gamma$). Further, an order $R_2 \leq R_1$ (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`) with $r$-power denominators in $R_1$ (`hR₂r`) and a map $\hat e : R_2 \to \operatorname{End}(A_0)$ over the base (`hê`) with `hE5a` (additivity, commutation with the $\Lambda$-action, level preservation), `hE5b1`–`hE5b3` (unitality, multiplicativity, rational integers), `hE5c` (norms: $\hat e(\bar x)\hat e(x)$ is multiplication by $\mathrm{nrd}(x)$), `hE5d` (compatibility of $\hat e$ with $e$ up to powers of $r$) and `hE5e` (a simultaneous matrix normalisation of the $e\gamma$ and the $\hat e x$ through a single $g$). A distinguished full level-$n$ point $P_0$ on $A_0$. Atkin–Lehner data at $\bar r$ on $A_0$: a curve $A_{0w}$, morphisms $a_w, a_w', b_w, b_w'$ with the stated compatibilities over the base, `hALw` (the pair $(a_w,a_w')$ exhibits $A_{0w}$ as the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$), `hBSw` and `hBSwlev` (the pair $(b_w,b_w')$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ preserving levels), and `hJOINTw` (a simultaneous normalisation as in `hE2` in which in addition the endomorphism $a_w$ followed by $b_w$ of $A_0$ is induced by an element matching $r^{k_w'}g\,\iota_0(\bar w)\,g^{-1}$).
--
--   **Drinfeld side.** A ring map $\iota : \mathbb Z_{r^2} \to O^{\mathrm{nr}}$; a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$, special for the structure map induced by $\iota$ (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`); a moduli package $\mathrm{MD}$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfying the Zariski sheaf condition (`hMD`); a map $\eta$ sending rigidified objects to points of $\mathrm{MD}$, with `hη` in three clauses (on admissible rigidified objects $\eta$ identifies points exactly with isomorphism of rigidified objects, $\eta$ is natural in the base, and every point of $\mathrm{MD}$ is locally on the base of the form $\eta(t)$ for admissible $t$); an injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action and $\varpi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image is commensurable with $M_2(\mathcal O)$ through a single power $r^{m}$ (`hE₀`). A family of maps $e_D$ from the $G$-functor of $\mathrm{MD}$ over $\mathcal O$ to the product of the functor corepresented by $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ with Drinfeld's functor $\Omega = \Omega(K_0,\pi)$ of Deligne data, together with `hnatD` (naturality), `hbijD` (bijectivity on each Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra in which $\pi$ is nilpotent), `hfstD` (the first component of $e_D(x)$ is the leg $x.\psi$), `hGLD` ($e_D$ turns the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action on $G$-points into the twisted action on pairs, i.e. Frobenius twist of the leg by $-\mathrm{vdet}(g)$ and pullback of the Deligne datum by $g^{-1}$), `hPiD` ($\varpi$-translation becomes Frobenius twist of the leg with unchanged datum) and `hPiexD` (existence of $\varpi$-translates). A reduction map $\kappa : O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi) \to O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ compatible with the quotient maps (`hκ`), an integer $n_0$ and a series $\beta_0$ which is an isogeny $\Phi \to \kappa_*X_0$ of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`).
--
--   **The comparison map $\Xi$.** A map $\Xi$ attaching to each rigidified curve over a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent and leg $\psi : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$ a $G$-point of $\mathrm{MD}$, subject to: `hΞleg` (for $B$ with only trivial idempotents the leg of $\Xi$ is a Frobenius twist $\mathrm{Fr}^{k}$ of $\psi$); `hΞnat` (compatibility with pullback of curves and rigidifications); `hΞiso` (invariance under isomorphisms of rigidified curves admitting a comparison of the reduction and auxiliary legs up to powers of $r$); `hΞdef` (for connected $B$ in which $r$ is nilpotent and a rigidified curve whose formal module structure is given by $X$ and $\theta$, there are $j \leq 1$ and a rigidified object $t$ with $t.X = X$, transported from $\theta_0,\kappa,\beta_0$ with exponent $j$, admissible for the leg $\mathrm{Fr}^{-j}\psi$, and $\Xi$ of the curve equals the triple consisting of that leg, the nilpotence of $r$ and $\eta(t)$). Finally an element $g_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ with `heqΓ` (over connected $B$, replacing a rigidification by its translate along $e\gamma$ corresponds to acting on $\Xi$ by $r^{c}\,g_0\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g_0^{-1}$ for some $c \in \mathbb Z$) and `heqW` (over connected $B$ in which $\bar r$ is invertible, passing from a curve to its Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ with matching rigidifications corresponds to acting by $r^{c}\,g_0\,\iota_0(\bar w)\,g_0^{-1}$).
--
--   **The functor $\mathrm{PR}$ and the period map.** A Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $C$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent (`hCπ`) together with a leg $\chi_C : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to C$; a functor $\mathrm{PR}$ from $C$-algebras to types, with no representability assumed; a point map $\mathrm{ptR}$ which to each $C$-algebra $S$ compatible with the $\mathcal O$-structure, each leg $\psi_S$ equal to $\chi_C$ followed by $C \to S$, each curve $u$ with full level $n$ over $S$ and each rigidification $\rho$ of $u.1$ relative to $A_0$ along $\psi_S$ assigns a point of $\mathrm{PR}(S)$. The laws: `hR2` (naturality of $\mathrm{ptR}$ under base change along $C$-algebra maps, for pullbacks compatible with the level point and the rigidification), `hR3s` (every point of $\mathrm{PR}(S)$ is $\mathrm{ptR}$ of some pair $(u,\rho)$), `hR3i` (over $S$ with only trivial idempotents, equality of two such points yields an isomorphism of the full-level curves together with comparison data on the rigidifications up to powers of $r$), `hR1` (conversely, such an isomorphism and comparison data force equality of the points). A family of maps $\theta$ from $\mathrm{PR}(S)$ to $\Omega(S)$ for Noetherian $S$, natural in $S$ (`hθnat`), with `hθ`: $\theta(\mathrm{ptR}(u,\rho))$ is the pullback along $(g_0^{-1})^{-1}$ of the Deligne-datum component of $e_D(\Xi(u.1,\rho))$.
--
--   Here a rigidification of a curve $E$ over $B$ along $\psi$ consists of a curve $E_b$ over $B/(\pi)$ with a morphism $g_b$ exhibiting it as the reduction of $E$, a curve $A_b$ over $B/(\pi)$ with a morphism $g_A$ exhibiting it as the pullback of $A_0$ along the residue leg, an integer $d$ and morphisms $\varphi : E_b \to A_b$, $\varphi' : A_b \to E_b$ forming an isogeny pair of degree $r^{d}$ preserving the level structure.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Let $S$ be a local Artinian ring with algebraically closed residue field, Noetherian, a $C$-algebra and an $\mathcal O$-algebra with compatible scalar towers, and let $S_0$ be a nontrivial Noetherian $C$-algebra and $\mathcal O$-algebra with compatible scalar towers. Let $p : S \to S_0$ be a surjective map of $C$-algebras whose kernel has square zero, in the form: any two elements of $S$ killed by $p$ have product $0$. Let $g \in G$, $j \in \{0,1\}$, $x_0 \in \mathrm{PR}(S_0)$ and $d$ a Deligne datum in $\Omega(S)$.
--
--   Assume first that $x_0$ admits a presentation of label $(g,j)$: there are a witness that $\pi$ is nilpotent in $S_0$, a leg $\psi_S : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to S_0$ equal to $\chi_C$ followed by $C \to S_0$, a curve $u$ with full level $n$ over $S_0$ and a rigidification $\rho$ of $u.1$ along $\psi_S$ such that $\mathrm{ptR}(u,\rho) = x_0$, such that for some full level-$n$ structure $P_n$ on $u.1$ the norm level transport condition relating $\mathrm{Fr}, \theta_0, \kappa, \beta_0, \Phi, \iota, \mathrm{coord}, P_0, \rho$ and $P_n$ holds and the level point of $u$ is the translate of $P_n$ by the action of $\chi(g)$, and such that the leg of $\Xi(u.1,\rho)$ is $\mathrm{Fr}^{-j}\psi_S$. Assume second that $\theta_{S_0}(x_0)$ is the image of $d$ under $\Omega(p)$.
--
--   Then $\pi$ is nilpotent in $S$ and in $S_0$, and there are a leg $\psi_S : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to S$ equal to $\chi_C$ followed by $C \to S$, with $p \circ \psi_S$ equal to $\chi_C$ followed by $C \to S_0$, a curve $u$ with full level $n$ over $S_0$ and a rigidification $\rho$ of $u.1$ along $p \circ \psi_S$ such that:
--
--   1. $\mathrm{ptR}(u,\rho) = x_0$ over $S_0$ with the leg $p \circ \psi_S$;
--
--   2. there is a full level-$n$ structure $P_n$ on $u.1$ satisfying the norm level transport condition for $\mathrm{Fr}, \theta_0, \kappa, \beta_0, \Phi, \iota, \mathrm{coord}, P_0$ and $\rho$, such that the level point of $u$ is the translate of $P_n$ under the action of $\chi(g)$;
--
--   3. there are a fake elliptic curve $E$ over $S$ and a rigidification $\varrho$ of $E$ along $\psi_S$ with $e_D(\Xi(E,\varrho))$ equal to the pair consisting of the leg $\mathrm{Fr}^{-j}\psi_S$ and the pullback of $d$ along $g_0^{-1}$; and
--
--   4. there are a curve $E'$ over $S_0$, a morphism $g_E : E'.A \to E.A$ exhibiting $E'$ as the pullback of $E$ along $p$, and a rigidification $\varrho'$ of $E'$ along $p \circ \psi_S$ which is the pullback of $\varrho$ via $g_E$, together with an isomorphism $i : u.1.A \cong E'.A$ over $S_0$ (so $i$ followed by the structure morphism of $E'$ is that of $u.1$) which is an isomorphism of fake elliptic curves, i.e. compatible with the group laws, with the $\Lambda$-actions, and with the level subschemes in both directions; and finally comparison data for the rigidifications: a morphism $i_b$ from the reduction curve of $\rho$ to that of $\varrho'$ with $i_b$ followed by $\varrho'.g_b$ equal to $\rho.g_b$ followed by $i$, and over the base, a morphism $u_A$ from the auxiliary curve of $\varrho'$ to that of $\rho$ which is a pullback along the identity and satisfies $u_A$ followed by $\rho.g_A$ equals $\varrho'.g_A$, and exponents $i_1, j_1$ such that $i_b$ followed by $\varrho'.\varphi$, then $u_A$, then multiplication by $r^{i_1}$ equals $\rho.\varphi$ followed by multiplication by $r^{j_1}$.
--
--   The curve $u$ and rigidification $\rho$ produced in the conclusion need not be those supplied in the assumption; what is asserted is that a presentation of $x_0$ with the same label can be chosen with its leg descending to $S$, and that the prescribed Deligne datum $d$ over $S$ is realised by a rigidified curve over $S$ whose reduction along $p$ is isomorphic to that presentation.
--
--   This is the existence half of the relative representability step in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of the quaternionic (Shimura) curve: for an Artinian local base $S$ with square-zero thickening datum $p : S \to S_0$, a point of the rigidified moduli functor over $S_0$ together with a prescribed period in Drinfeld's space over $S$ is lifted to a rigidified fake elliptic curve over $S$, compatibly with the given level label $(g,j)$. It is used to establish the corresponding statement for the family of $\Omega$-valued points, and so feeds the comparison between the $p$-adic analytic uniformisation and the integral model of the Shimura curve at the prime $r$.
